WEBVTT

00:11:58.525 --> 00:12:00.529
on what's called the passion tax,

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:02.283
where Aaron Kay and his colleagues

00:12:02.307 --> 00:12:04.759
have found that people who love their jobs

00:12:04.783 --> 00:12:08.267
are more likely to get asked
to do extra work unpaid,

00:12:08.291 --> 00:12:10.015
even if it's not part of their role,

00:12:10.039 --> 00:12:11.831
even if it's demeaning.

00:12:11.855 --> 00:12:13.618
And they end up sacrificing sleep,

00:12:13.642 --> 00:12:16.363
family time and health because of it.

00:12:16.387 --> 00:12:19.729
Do you feel like there was
a passion tax imposed at WeWork?

00:12:20.339 --> 00:12:22.392
DF: I think people loved what they did.

00:12:24.108 --> 00:12:25.802
And I think they worked hard.

00:12:26.498 --> 00:12:31.279
You know, I think if you asked
most people that worked there